# Inbound interrupt packets from a live Zen Studio+ panel start-up (hardware session 2, 2026-09-15),
# one per line as hex, 320 bytes each, exactly as read. Two slices of device-to-host completions:
#   1. the 120-packet window richest in replies (0x75), among the device’s 0x73/0x83 state reports;
#   2. 10 packets around the one refusal (0x80000075: the request id with the top bit set).
# The slices are not adjacent in the capture; each report is whole, so replaying them in order is valid.
# Regenerate: gazelle-capture import <start-up capture> --vid 0x23e5 --pid 0xa100 > events.jsonl, then
# keep interrupt IN completions and cut those two windows.


































































































































